meta {
  name: Boot sound off
  type: http
  seq: 26
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/bootsound?on=0
  body: none
  auth: none
}

docs {
  200 { bootSound: false }

  Read-or-set, same shape as /beep. GET /bootsound reports the current
  value; POST /bootsound?on=1 re-enables.

  Separate from /beep on purpose: /beep silences the per-press tick,
  this one silences the power-up chime. Either can be off alone.

  Stored under its own NVS key ("wifi"/"bootsnd"), NOT in the cfg blob —
  adding a field to Config changes sizeof(Config) and loadConfig deletes
  any blob whose size does not match. Default is ON when the key is
  absent, so a new device plays the chime at power-up.

  Takes effect at the NEXT boot: the setting is read in loadConfig(),
  which runs before soundStartup(). Turning it off does not make the
  current boot silent retroactively.
}
